    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that after `skip()` hits EOF on a size-0 `NullReader` (setting the internal `eof` flag), a subsequent `read(char[])` throws `IOException(\"Read after end of file\")`.\n\nLet me write a clearer version with better names and a descriptive test method name.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version renames `nullReader0` to `sizeZeroReader` and `charArray0` to `buffer` for clarity, renames the test method to `test_readAfterSkipPastEndOfFile_throwsIOException`, and adds a brief Javadoc comment explaining why skipping on a size-0 reader immediately triggers the EOF flag that causes the subsequent read to throw."
    }
